# Cron Job Cards Guide

## Overview
This folder documents cron job cards for blog system. Each card captures the intent, scope, schedule and notes.

Format (per week/month):

- Title: `[YYYY-MM]-BLOG_CRON_ENTRY.md` or `2026-W{W}-Weekly-Blog-Cron`
  - YYYY-Month style entries cover full month; W-{Week} covers specific weeks.
- Schema:
```yaml
---
id: "cron-a1b2c3d4"
title: "[YYYY-MM] Blog Cron Entry for Week(s)"
status: active | draft | deprecated

# High-level intent and scope (short)
intent_scope:

schedule_weeks_or_months_as_range_if_not_daily_cron jobs_run_on:
  - KR
- time_zone_hint_seconds_offset_utc_plus_9 = +32400 sec.

content_plan_summary_cards_to_create_for_this_period: optional, but useful for multi-week planning

notes_and_optional_additional_context_from_human_when_available:

---
```

## Weekly Entry (Aug‑Sep)
```yaml
# Example 2026-AUG-W31-Weekly-Blog-Cron.md content:
id: "cron-a1b2c3d4"
title: "[YYYY-MM] Blog Cron — Aug Week(s) W{W}"
status: active

intent_scope:

schedule_weeks_or_months_as_range_if_not_daily_cron jobs_run_on_KR - 6pm KR (09 UTC)
- time_zone_hint_seconds_offset_utc_plus_9 = +32400 sec.

content_plan_summary_cards_to_create_for_this_period:
# optional
notes_and_optional_additional_context_from_human_when_available:

---
```

## Usage

1. Check this guide for current format.
2. Use weekly/monthly templates as a starting point (e.g., Aug‑Sep 2026).
3. Keep notes concise; link to relevant docs/CRDs where appropriate.

When in doubt, use the template above and adapt labels/context accordingly without guessing dates or offsets beyond what’s provided here.


